---
// Home-page story: a sticky 3D token field; a self-portrait, then the bio told in four chapters.
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import fig1 from '../data/fig1.json';
import { LEGEND, legendHTML } from '../scripts/token-field/legend';
const scenes = fig1.scenes;
// Papers for the Chapter 0 cards, newest first.
const papers = (await getCollection('publications'))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.localeCompare(a.data.date))
  .map((p) => ({ id: p.id, title: p.data.title, venue: p.data.venue, year: p.data.year, thumb: p.data.thumb }));
const tEnd = fig1.video.frames[fig1.video.frames.length - 1].t; // the last frame is "now"
---
<section class="story" aria-label="Introduction" data-papers={JSON.stringify(papers)}>
  <div class="stage" data-stage>
    <canvas class="field" data-canvas aria-label="Interactive 3D field of image tokens. Hover to query a token, drag to change viewpoint, click to send a ripple."></canvas>
    <img class="fallback" src="/img/profile.jpeg" alt="" />

    <div class="qlabel" data-qlabel hidden><span class="mono">Q</span> <span data-qtext></span></div>
    <div class="ctag mono" data-ctag hidden></div>
    <!-- Chapter 0: lines from the retrieval heads to where they look, the model's box, the hand-labeled box. -->
    <svg class="vlayer" data-vlayer aria-hidden="true">
      <g data-vlines></g>
      <polygon class="gt" data-vgt />
      <polygon class="pred" data-vpred />
    </svg>
    <div class="bubble" data-bubble hidden>hey — my glasses!</div>
    <div class="mtag mono" data-mtag hidden></div>
    <div class="vrh stage-vrh mono" data-vrh hidden></div>
    <ul class="legend stage-legend mono" data-legend aria-label="What the marks mean" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[0])}></ul>
    <div class="boxtag mono" data-boxtag="0" hidden></div>
    <div class="boxtag mono" data-boxtag="1" hidden></div>
    {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5].map((i) => <div class="ftag mono" data-ftag={i} hidden></div>)}
    <!-- Chapter IV: the clip the five frames came from; it plays as the live plate of tokens. -->
    <video class="clip" data-clip src="/fig1/video/clip.mp4" muted playsinline preload="none" aria-hidden="true"></video>

    <ol class="rail mono" aria-hidden="true">
      <li data-rail="0">0</li><li data-rail="1">I</li><li data-rail="2">II</li><li data-rail="3">III</li><li data-rail="4">IV</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="hud">
      <div class="picker" role="group" aria-label="Choose an image">
        {scenes.map((s, i) => (
          <button type="button" data-scene={i} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-label={`Image: ${s.id}`}>
            <img src={s.image} alt="" />
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="credit mono" data-credit>{scenes[0].credit} · {scenes[0].grid[0]}×{scenes[0].grid[1]} tokens</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chapters">
    <article class="chapter c0" data-chapter="0">
      <div class="card">
        <!-- Phones: the heads panel appears here, right under the photo, once something on it is tapped. -->
        <div class="vrh card-vrh mono" data-vrh></div>
        <p class="kicker mono">KAIST Visual AI Group · Graduate School of Metaverse</p>
        <h1 class="title">Chanho<br />Park</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Can multimodal models actually <em>use</em> what they see — and can we verify that they do?
        </p>
        <p class="meta mono">
          M.S. student advised by <a href="https://mhsung.github.io/">Prof. Minhyuk Sung</a>
        </p>
        <p class="venues mono">
          {papers.map((p, i) => <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={`/papers/#${p.id}`}>{p.venue} ’{String(p.year).slice(2)}</a></>)}
        </p>
        <p class="live" data-live="0" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <ul class="legend card-legend mono" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[0])}></ul>
        <p class="hint mono"><span class="dot"></span> move · click · swipe · scroll ↓</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="chapter" data-chapter="1">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="bio">
        <p class="num mono">I. The question</p>
        <p>
          My research asks whether multimodal models can actually use the information available to them—and how we
          can verify that they do. Spatial information may be present in an image yet encoded in a form that a model
          cannot effectively exploit.
        </p>
        </div>
        <div class="inst">
        <ul class="legend card-legend mono" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[1])}></ul>
        <div class="probe">
          <div class="chips" data-pchips role="group" aria-label="Questions"></div>
          <p class="answer" data-panswer aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
        <p class="live" data-live="1" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="fig mono"><b>Fig. 1.</b> Same photo, two questions: one in the camera’s frame, one from another point of view. Answers and top-20 retrieval-head attention from Qwen2.5-VL-7B (MLX 4-bit, run locally); boxes and ground truth are hand-labeled.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="chapter" data-chapter="2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="bio">
        <p class="num mono">II. Use</p>
        <p>
          In <a href="/papers/#apc">Perspective-Aware Reasoning</a> and <a href="/papers/#token-warping">Token
          Warping</a>, I address this by transforming the representations that models reason over rather than the
          pixels themselves.
        </p>
        </div>
        <div class="inst">
        <ul class="legend card-legend mono" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[2])}></ul>
        <p class="live" data-live="2" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="fig mono"><b>Fig. 2.</b> Token warping, live: each token is placed by its estimated depth (Depth Anything V2) and turned to face the camera — nothing is re-rendered. Drag for another nearby viewpoint (±25°).</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="chapter" data-chapter="3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="bio">
        <p class="num mono">III. Verify</p>
        <p>
          But improved accuracy alone does not show that a model relied on the right evidence. In <a
          href="/papers/#vrh">Retrieval Heads Meet Vision</a>, I identify a small set of attention heads—<strong>Visual
          Retrieval Heads</strong>—that carry visual evidence, and causally test their role in grounding by masking them.
        </p>
        </div>
        <div class="inst">
        <ul class="legend card-legend mono" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[3])}></ul>
        <div class="probe" data-probe>
          <div class="chips" data-chips role="group" aria-label="Questions"></div>
          <div class="views mono" data-views role="group" aria-label="Attention heads"></div>
          <label class="switch mono">
            <input type="checkbox" data-mask />
            <span class="track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            mask retrieval heads
          </label>
          <p class="answer" data-answer aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
        <p class="live" data-live="3" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="fig mono"><b>Fig. 3.</b> Attention from the question to image tokens. <span data-provenance>Loading attention extracted from Qwen2.5-VL-7B…</span></p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="chapter" data-chapter="4">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="bio">
        <p class="num mono">IV. Over time</p>
        <p>
          I am now extending this line of inquiry over time: asking what long-horizon models should retain in memory,
          when stale internal states should be revised, and how these mechanisms can support multimodal agents that
          perceive, reason, and interact in real-world environments.
        </p>
        </div>
        <div class="inst">
        <ul class="legend card-legend mono" set:html={legendHTML(LEGEND[4])}></ul>
        <div class="player" data-player>
          <button type="button" class="play mono" data-play aria-label="Play the video">▶</button>
          <div class="track-wrap">
            <input class="seek" type="range" min="0" max={tEnd} step="0.01" value={tEnd} data-seek aria-label="Video time (seconds)" />
            <div class="thumbs">
              {fig1.video.frames.map((f, i) => (
                <button type="button" data-thumb-frame={i} style={`left: ${(100 * f.t) / tEnd}%`} aria-label={`Frame ${i + 1}, ${f.t.toFixed(1)} s`}>
                  <img src={f.image} alt="" />
                  <span class="mono">{i + 1}</span>
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="tnow mono" data-tnow>{tEnd.toFixed(1)} s</span>
        </div>
        <div class="probe">
          <p class="qline mono">Q · {fig1.video.question} <span class="qwhen" data-qwhen>asked at t = {tEnd.toFixed(1)} s</span></p>
          <label class="switch mono">
            <input type="checkbox" data-memmask />
            <span class="track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            mask retrieval heads
          </label>
          <p class="answer" data-memanswer aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
        <p class="live" data-live="4" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="fig mono"><b>Fig. 4.</b> <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bombus_terrestris_rolling_ball.webm">A bumblebee rolling a ball</a> (CC BY 4.0) plays as tokens; every 1.5 s a frame drops into memory — the five frames the model is given. <span data-memprov>Loading attention extracted from Qwen2.5-VL-7B…</span></p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { mountStory } from '../scripts/token-field/story';
  mountStory();
</script>

<style>
  .story { position: relative; }
  .stage {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 0; height: 100vh; height: 100svh; overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0 calc(50% - 50vw);
  }
  .stage:global(.c0) .field { cursor: grab; }
  .bubble {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: none; white-space: nowrap;
    translate: -50% calc(-100% - 14px); font: 500 .85rem var(--font-body);
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 14px; padding: .3rem .75rem;
    animation: pop .25s ease-out;
  }
  .bubble::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: -6px; width: 10px; height: 10px; background: var(--bg);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(45deg);
  }
  @keyframes pop { from { scale: .6; opacity: 0; } }
  .stage:global(.c0.knockable) .field { cursor: pointer; }
  /* Chapter 0 readouts on the photo: the model's answers right next to what they are about. */
  .mtag {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: none; display: grid; gap: .18rem; min-width: 13.5rem;
    font-size: .66rem; line-height: 1.35; color: var(--ink); translate: -50% 0;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 88%, transparent); backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; padding: .45rem .65rem;
  }
  .mtag[hidden] { display: none; }
  .mtag :global(.t) { color: var(--muted); font-size: .6rem; letter-spacing: .02em; }
  .mtag :global(.r) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: .8rem; }
  .mtag :global(i) { font-style: normal; color: var(--muted); }
  .mtag :global(b) { font-weight: 500; margin-left: .25rem; }
  .mtag :global(.ok) { color: var(--muted); }
  .mtag :global(.bad) { color: var(--accent); }

  /* Chapter 0 overlay: head → token lines (attention), the model's box (accent), the hand-labeled box (dashed ink). */
  .vlayer { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; overflow: visible; }
  .vlayer :global(path) { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1; opacity: .55; }
  .vlayer polygon { fill: none; opacity: 0; transition: opacity .25s; }
  .vlayer polygon:global(.on) { opacity: 1; }
  .vlayer .gt { stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .vlayer .pred { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.2; }

  /* The model's 784 attention heads (28 layers × 28 heads); the 20 retrieval heads lit. */
  .vrh { font-size: .64rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--ink); display: flex; gap: .9rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  .vrh[hidden] { display: none; }
  .stage-vrh {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: auto; padding: .6rem .7rem; border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 82%, transparent); backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--rule) 70%, transparent);
  }
  .card-vrh { display: none; }
  .vrh :global(.grid) { flex: none; display: block; }
  .vrh :global(.grid rect) { fill: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink) 9%, transparent); }
  .vrh :global(.grid rect.v) { fill: var(--accent); }
  .vrh :global(.grid rect.v.off) { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1; }
  .vrh :global(.grid rect.r) { fill: var(--ink); }
  .vrh :global(.grid rect.r.off) { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1; }
  .vrh :global(.side) { display: grid; gap: .35rem; min-width: 12.5rem; max-width: 15rem; }
  .vrh :global(.t) { color: var(--muted); }
  .vrh :global(.q) { font: 400 .82rem/1.35 var(--font-body); }
  .vrh :global(.seg) { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .25rem; }
  .vrh :global(.seg button) {
    all: unset; cursor: pointer; padding: .18rem .5rem; border-radius: 99px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted);
  }
  .vrh :global(.seg button:hover) { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--muted); }
  .vrh :global(.seg button[aria-pressed='true']) { background: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); }
  .vrh :global(.seg button:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .vrh :global(.res b) { font-weight: 500; }
  .vrh :global(.res .ok) { color: var(--ink); }
  .vrh :global(.res .bad) { color: var(--accent); }
  .vrh :global(.res .part) { color: var(--ink); opacity: .75; }
  .vrh :global(.key) { color: var(--muted); font-size: .58rem; }
  .vrh :global(.key i) { display: inline-block; width: .9rem; height: .55rem; vertical-align: -1px; margin-right: .25rem; }
  .vrh :global(.key .kp) { border: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .vrh :global(.key .kg) { border: 1px dashed var(--ink); }
  .stage:global(.c0) .stage-legend, .stage:global(.c0) .credit { display: none; } /* the heads panel takes that corner */
  .field { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: pan-y; cursor: crosshair; }
  .fallback { display: none; }
  .stage.no-webgl .field { display: none; }
  .stage.no-webgl .fallback {
    display: block; position: absolute; right: 6vw; top: 50%; translate: 0 -50%; width: min(46vw, 640px);
    border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  /* Labels that follow 3D positions */
  .qlabel {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: none;
    max-width: min(30rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)); text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;
    translate: -50% calc(-100% - 18px);
    font: 500 .8rem var(--font-body); padding: .35rem .7rem; border-radius: 99px;
    background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); box-shadow: 0 6px 24px -10px var(--accent);
  }
  .qlabel .mono { font: 500 .65rem var(--font-mono); opacity: .8; }
  .ctag {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: none; white-space: nowrap;
    translate: 14px 14px; font-size: .66rem; color: var(--ink);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 85%, transparent); border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: .2rem .45rem; border-radius: 3px; backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  }

  /* Legend: one mark = one meaning across the story */
  .legend { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: .64rem; line-height: 1.35; color: var(--muted); }
  .legend :global(li) { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .55rem; margin: .32rem 0; }
  .legend :global(.sw) { flex: none; width: 1.15rem; height: .8rem; position: relative; display: inline-block; }
  .legend :global(.sw-tile) { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8aa06a, #c9a46a); border-radius: 1px; }
  .legend :global(.sw-outline) { border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 1px; }
  .legend :global(.sw-heat) { background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--heat-1), var(--heat-3), var(--heat-4)); border-radius: 1px; }
  .legend :global(.sw-line) { height: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--accent); width: 1.15rem; }
  .legend :global(.sw-box) { border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: transparent; }
  .legend :global(.sw-gap) {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #b9a98c 0 40%, transparent 40% 60%, #b9a98c 60%); border-radius: 1px;
  }
  .legend :global(.sw-depth) {
    background: linear-gradient(#b9a98c, #b9a98c) 0 100% / 40% 55% no-repeat, linear-gradient(#8a7b62, #8a7b62) 100% 0 / 40% 100% no-repeat;
  }
  .legend :global(.sw-stack) {
    background: linear-gradient(#b9a98c, #b9a98c) 0 100% / 60% 60% no-repeat, linear-gradient(#d8cdb8, #d8cdb8) 100% 0 / 60% 60% no-repeat;
  }
  .legend :global(.sw-ink) { background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, var(--ink) 0 2px, transparent 2px 4px); opacity: .55; border-radius: 1px; }
  .legend :global(.sw-paper) { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #c9a46a 0 50%, #cfc8bb 50%); border-radius: 1px; }
  .legend :global(.sw-fade) { background: #b9a98c; opacity: .3; border-radius: 1px; }
  .stage-legend {
    position: absolute; right: max(1rem, calc(50vw - 33rem)); bottom: 5.6rem; width: 17.5rem;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 80%, transparent); padding: .5rem .7rem; border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--rule) 70%, transparent); backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  }
  .card-legend { display: none; }

  .boxtag, .ftag {
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; pointer-events: none; white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: .62rem; color: var(--ink); translate: 0 calc(-100% - 6px);
  }
  .boxtag { background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 80%, transparent); padding: .1rem .35rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .ftag { color: var(--muted); background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 78%, transparent); padding: 0 .3rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .ftag.now { color: var(--accent); }

  .live {
    margin: 1.1rem 0 1rem !important; padding: .55rem 0 .55rem .8rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font: 400 .92rem/1.5 var(--font-body); color: var(--ink);
    min-height: 3em; transition: opacity .2s;
  }
  .live:empty { display: none; }
  /* Chapter 0's line changes length as you point and knock; a fixed box keeps the name from jumping. */
  .c0 .live { min-height: 8.6rem; }
  .live :global(b) { font: 500 .82rem var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); }
  .live :global(i) { font-style: italic; }

  .rail {
    position: absolute; left: max(1rem, calc(50vw - 33rem)); bottom: 2rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none;
    display: flex; gap: .9rem; font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .rail li { transition: color .3s; }
  .rail li.on { color: var(--accent); }
  .rail li.on::before { content: '— '; }

  .hud { position: absolute; right: max(1rem, calc(50vw - 33rem)); bottom: 1.6rem; text-align: right; }
  .picker { display: flex; gap: .4rem; justify-content: flex-end; transition: opacity .3s; }
  .picker:global(.off) { opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .picker button {
    all: unset; cursor: pointer; width: 3.1rem; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); opacity: .55; transition: opacity .2s, transform .2s, border-color .2s;
  }
  .picker button:hover { opacity: .9; transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .picker button[aria-pressed='true'] { opacity: 1; border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent); }
  .picker button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .picker img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .credit { margin: .45rem 0 0; font-size: .62rem; color: var(--muted); }

  /* Chapters scroll over the sticky stage */
  .chapters { position: relative; z-index: 1; margin-top: -100vh; margin-top: -100svh; pointer-events: none; }
  .chapter { min-height: 100vh; min-height: 100svh; display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .chapter + .chapter { min-height: 115vh; }
  .card { pointer-events: auto; max-width: 27rem; }
  .card p { margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .card a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .card strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .chapter:not(.c0) .card {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--bg) 82%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--rule) 70%, transparent);
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem .6rem;
  }

  .kicker { font-size: .68rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .title {
    font: 400 clamp(3.6rem, 9vw, 7.2rem)/0.92 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: .2rem 0 1.4rem;
  }
  /* The research question is the page's main message: set large, right under the name. */
  .lede {
    font: 400 clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.25rem)/1.18 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.01em; max-width: 27rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }
  .meta { font-size: .72rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .meta a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
  .venues { font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .02em; color: var(--muted); }
  .venues a { color: var(--ink) !important; text-decoration: none !important; }
  .venues a:hover { color: var(--accent) !important; }
  .hint { margin-top: 2.2rem !important; font-size: .68rem; color: var(--muted); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; }
  .dot { width: .45rem; height: .45rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); animation: pulse 1.8s infinite; }
  @keyframes pulse { 50% { opacity: .25; } }

  .num { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
  .fig { font-size: .66rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: .7rem; }
  .fig b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }

  .probe { margin: 1.2rem 0 1.1rem; }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .35rem; }
  .chips :global(button) {
